Subject: [PATCH v3 2/2] lab-process-mail: Answer one message per run
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: orskzzltnpnptlnqysyzllwlyqvuvtrk
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 03:23:05 +0000

lab-process-mail looped until the inbox was empty, which made it a
daemon of its own inside the one lab-process-maild runs. A run that
answers one message and exits is simpler to reason about, and leaves
the decision of when to run again to the daemon.

lab-process-maild now runs it again at once while the inbox still has
mail, and sleeps only once it is empty, so a batch of mail is still
answered back to back. Running lab-process-mail by hand answers the
oldest message and nothing more.
